</li>
<li>
<p>distinguish degree distributions from power laws;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>understand configuration models;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>recognize assortative and disassortative mixing;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>understand homophily conceptually;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>understand community structure;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>define modularity conceptually;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>understand community detection;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>recognize hierarchical networks;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>understand bipartite networks;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>recognize projections of bipartite networks;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>understand multilayer and multiplex networks;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>recognize temporal networks;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>understand network robustness;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>recognize node and edge failures;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>understand percolation conceptually;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>recognize cascading failures;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>understand epidemic spreading on networks;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>recognize threshold effects;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>understand bond and site percolation conceptually;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>understand diffusion on networks;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>formulate Laplacian diffusion equations;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>understand random walks on graphs;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>construct transition matrices;</p>
</li>
<li>
